# REGRESSION (`todo/t0841`, R48 Track D1) — SANITIZER lane. The value-lane twin
# is `tests/fixtures/cow_comprehension_invariant_owned_name.gg`: same program,
# different instrument.
#
# Both lanes are needed. A value lane cannot tell a double-free from a correct
# run when the abort lands after the last print, and this program printed
# `ababab` before aborting.
#
# A COMPREHENSION IS A LOOP. `[s for i in 0..3]` evaluates `s` once per
# iteration exactly as `for i in 0..3: parts.push(s)` does, and the accumulate
# is a consuming position, so AGENTS.md § "Ownership at Consuming Positions"
# applies unchanged: *"Borrow, OR owned but live past this call → clone before
# call"*. The defect was upstream of the accumulate, in the liveness producer:
# the three comprehension arms of `src/ir/lowering/liveness.rs` recorded
# last-use in a SINGLE pass while the statement-loop arms did a two-pass
# back-edge dance, so the loop-invariant `s` was marked dead at its only
# syntactic use and MOVED on every iteration.
#
# RED-VERIFIED at pre-fix HEAD under `--sanitize`:
#
#   ERROR: AddressSanitizer: attempting double-free
#       #1 __gorget_global_dealloc_fn  #2 gorget_string_free
#       #3 gorget_array_free           #4 main
#
# ⚠ THE PAYLOAD MUST BE HEAP-FORCED (`mk("a","b")`, not a literal) or the
# double free is invisible: a literal is an immortal `.rodata` view with no
# destructor to run twice.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s = mk("a", "b")
    Vector[String] parts = [s for i in 0..3]
    print("".join(parts))
